  "description": "BAGWAK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C156 H198 Dy6 N12 Ni7 O66 2+,4(C1 H4 O1),9(H2 O1),2(H1 O1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1B (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2B (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3B (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.271-4.429 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.56-132.84°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [C156H198Dy6N12Ni7O66]2+·4MeOH·9H2O·2OH−. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Explicit bracketed charge: 2+.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
